00;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">ºÆ-ªéªÇºÁªéªîº©ªà, º║º¥º¥ªÇº┤º©º¢º░ªåº©ªÅ º┐º¥º╗º©ªéº©º║º©.<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">ºÆªïªüªéªâº┐º╗ºÁº¢º©ºÁ º▓ º║º░ªçºÁªüªéº▓ºÁ ªüº┐º╗º¥ªçºÁº¢º¢º¥º│º¥ ªÇºÁº│º©º¥º¢º░º╗ªîº¢º¥º│º¥ º║º╗º©º╝º░ªéº©ªçºÁªüº║º¥º│º¥ º▒º╗º¥º║º░ º¢º░ º▒ªâº┤ªâªëº©ªà º║º¥º¢ªäºÁªÇºÁº¢ªåº©ªÅªà COP º┐º¥ºÀº▓º¥º╗º©ªé ªüªéªÇº░º¢º░º╝ ºĞºÁº¢ªéªÇº░º╗ªîº¢º¥º╣ ºÉºÀº©º© º▒º¥º╗ºÁºÁ ªıªäªäºÁº║ªéº©º▓º¢º¥ º¥ªéªüªéº░º©º▓º░ªéªî ªüº▓º¥º© º¥º▒ªëº©ºÁ º©º¢ªéºÁªÇºÁªüªï, º¥ªüº¥º▒ºÁº¢º¢º¥ º▓ º¥ªéº¢º¥ªêºÁº¢º©º© º╝ºÁºÂº┤ªâº¢º░ªÇº¥º┤º¢º¥º╣ º┐º¥º┤º┤ºÁªÇºÂº║º© º©º¢º©ªåº©º░ªéº©º▓ º┐º¥ º░º┤º░º┐ªéº░ªåº©º© º║ º©ºÀº╝ºÁº¢ºÁº¢º©ªÄ º║º╗º©º╝º░ªéº░.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"><i>ºùº░º║º╗ªÄªçºÁº¢º©ºÁ<\\/i><\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">º¡º║º¥º╗º¥º│º©ªçºÁªüº║º░ªÅ º┐º¥º╗º©ªéº©º║º░ º▓ ºĞºÁº¢ªéªÇº░º╗ªîº¢º¥º╣ ºÉºÀº©º© ªÇºÁªêº©ªéºÁº╗ªîº¢º¥ º┐ªÇºÁº▓ªÇº░ªéº©º╗º░ªüªî º©ºÀ º┐ªÇºÁº©º╝ªâªëºÁªüªéº▓ºÁº¢º¢º¥ º│ªâº╝º░º¢º©ªéº░ªÇº¢º¥º╣ º┐ªÇº¥º▒º╗ºÁº╝ªï º▓ ªüªéªÇº░ªéºÁº│º©ªçºÁªüº║ªâªÄ º¥ªüº¢º¥º▓ªâ ªÇºÁº│º©º¥º¢º░º╗ªîº¢º¥º│º¥ ªÇº░ºÀº▓º©ªéº©ªÅ.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;border-left:none;border-top:none;border-right:none;border-bottom:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">ºŞº┐ªïªé ªÇºÁº│º©º¥º¢º░ º┐º¥º║º░ºÀªïº▓º░ºÁªé, ªçªéº¥<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">ªéªÇº░º¢ªüº│ªÇº░º¢º©ªçº¢ªïº╣<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">ªıº║º¥º╗º¥º│º©ªçºÁªüº║º©ºÁ º┐ªÇº¥º▒º╗ºÁº╝ªï º╗ªâªçªêºÁ º▓ªüºÁº│º¥ ªÇºÁªêº░ªéªî º¢ºÁ º┐º¥ªüªÇºÁº┤ªüªéº▓º¥º╝ º║º¥º¢º║ªâªÇºÁº¢ªåº©º©, º░ º┐º¥ªüªÇºÁº┤ªüªéº▓º¥º╝ ªüº¥ªéªÇªâº┤º¢º©ªçºÁªüªéº▓º░ º© ªüº©º¢ºÁªÇº│º©º©. º¡ªéº¥ªé º┐º¥º┤ªàº¥º┤ º┐ªÇºÁº┤º╗º░º│º░ºÁªé ªâº▒ºÁº┤º©ªéºÁº╗ªîº¢ªïºÁ º┤º¥º║º░ºÀº░ªéºÁº╗ªîªüªéº▓º░ ªéº¥º│º¥, ªçªéº¥ ºĞºÁº¢ªéªÇº░º╗ªîº¢º░ªÅ ºÉºÀº©ªÅ º¢ºÁ ªÅº▓º╗ªÅºÁªéªüªÅ l<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">ºŞº¢º│ºÁªÇ º┐ªÇº¥ªüªéº¥ º▓º¥ªüº┐ªÇº©º¢º©º╝º░ºÁªéªüªÅ º║º░º║ ªÇºÁº│º©º¥º¢, ªâªÅºÀº▓º©º╝ªïº╣ º┤º╗ªÅ º║º╗º©º╝º░ªéº©ªçºÁªüº║º©ªà ªÇº©ªüº║º¥º▓. ºÆº╝ºÁªüªéº¥ ªıªéº¥º│º¥ º¥º¢ º▓ªüºÁ º▒º¥º╗ªîªêºÁ º┐ªÇºÁº▓ªÇº░ªëº░ºÁªéªüªÅ º▓ º┐ªÇº¥ªüªéªÇº░º¢ªüªéº▓º¥ º▓º¥ºÀº╝º¥ºÂº¢º¥ªüªéºÁº╣, º│º┤ºÁ ªäº¥ªÇº╝º©ªÇªâºÁªéªüªÅ º¢º¥º▓º░ªÅ º╝º¥º┤ºÁº╗ªî ªâªüªéº¥º╣ªçº©º▓º¥º│º¥ ªÇº░ºÀº▓º©ªéº©ªÅ, º║º¥ªéº¥ªÇº░ªÅ º╝º¥º│º╗º░ º▒ªï º┐º¥ªüº╗ªâºÂº©ªéªî º┐ªÇº©º╝ºÁªÇº¥º╝ º┤º╗ªÅ º▒º¥º╗ºÁºÁ ªêº©ªÇº¥º║º¥º│º¥ ºÁº▓ªÇº░ºÀº©º╣ªüº║º¥º│º¥ ªÇºÁº│º©º¥º¢º░.<\\/span><\\/p>\",\"en\":\"<p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\" class=\\\"docData;DOCY;v5;29809;\\\\\\\\\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Central Asia is undergoing a profound environmental transformation driven by both climate-related threats and a new political reality. This article examines the regionÔÇÖs growing consolidation in search of collective responses to <\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">transboundary<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> environmental challenges. The environmental agenda of 2025ÔÇô2026 has moved beyond a <\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">secondary policy issue to become a central instrument of green diplomacy. It also explores the prospects for regional cooperation as a strategic foundation for implementing comprehensive measures aimed at ecosystem preservation and sustainable development.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">The integration dynamics unfolding across Central Asia have triggered a broad socio-economic renaissance throughout the region. Rapid economic growth, accelerated urbanization, and expanding i<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">ndustrial capacity have delivered undeniable benefits, including higher living standards, increased investment, and stronger trade. At the same time, this progress has come at a growing environmental cost that is increasingly affecting the quality of life.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Today, the region f<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">aces a paradox: its economic achievements are becoming constrained by mounting environmental pressures, requiring both strategic reflection and effective policy responses. This challenge is by no means unique to Central Asia; rather, it forms part of a bro<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">ader global trend. As part of the ongoing global reset, countries around the world are reassessing their development strategies, embracing ESG (Environmental, Social, and Governance) principles and adapting to the emerging landscape of green protectionism.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Recognizing its position at the center of this transformation, Central AsiaÔÇölong situated on the margins of international climate discussionsÔÇöis steadily moving to the forefront. This shift reflects the growing understanding that <\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">transboundary<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> challenges, from glacier retreat to severe urban air pollution, transcend national borders and require coordinated regional action.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"><i>Looking Back: From Fragmentation to Regional Coordination<\\/i><\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">The past decade has witnessed a gradual<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> but fundamental shift in how Central Asian countries approach environmental challenges. The region has evolved from being largely a recipient of international environmental assistance into an increasingly proactive contributor to global climate solutions.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">A major catalyst for this transformation was the adoption of the Paris Agreement, which prompted the countries of the region to assess national climate risks and mode<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">rnize their environmental legislation. Equally significant was the revival of dialogue within the International Fund for Saving the Aral Sea (IFAS), marking a transition from an era of \\\"water disputes\\\" toward recognition of shared environmental challenges.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">The Consultative Meetings of the Heads of State of Central Asia elevated environmental issues to the highest political level, representing a genuine diplomatic breakthrough for regional cooperation.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">The Regional Environm<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">ental Centre for Central Asia (CAREC) has emerged as the region\'s leading expert platform, bringing together governments, academia, and civil society to implement hundreds of pilot projects focused on climate adaptation and sustainable resource management.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Large-scale national afforestation initiatives such as <\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Yashil<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> <\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Makon<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> in Uzbekistan and <\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Zhasyl<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> <\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Beldeu<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> in Kazakhstan have also acquired a regional dimension, serving as coordinated responses to dust storms, land degradation, and desertification.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Collectively, these and other initiatives have gradually shifted the regional agenda from discussing environmental problems toward coordinating practical measures to attract technology, financing, and international expertise.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">At the same time, Central Asian countries have begun implementing major renewable energy projects in parallel, viewing clean energy as an essential means of reducing pressure on ecosystems while decreasing reliance on thermal power generation.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">The increasingly coordinated participation of Central Asian delegations at the United Nations Climate Change Conferences (COP) has transformed the region into an increasingly influential voice within global climate governance.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Perhaps the most significant achievement has been overcoming decades of mistrust over shared natural res<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">ources. A unique framework of regional cooperation has emerged, in which environmental cooperation has become a form of soft power, uniting the five Central Asian states around a common objective: preserving their shared environment for future generations.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"><i>The Global Reset and Future Horizons<\\/i><\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Central Asia has now entered a new phase characterized by a transition from re<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">gional consolidation to deeper integration into the global environmental agenda. The global reset in climate governance is establishing new rules, where climate resilience is becoming as valuable a strategic asset as natural resources or transit potential.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Within the region, new challenges have also emergedÔÇöparticularly those associated with the environmental cost of rising living standards. Rapid motorization, the operation of thermal power plants at peak capacity, and the expansion of <\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">peri<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">-urban agricultural production have significantly worsened air quality, turning smog into a serious public health concern for the region\'s largest cities.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Addressing these challenges requires far more than installing pollution-control equipment. It demands an integrated regional approach based on close coordination among the water, energy, and food sectors across national borders.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Against this backdrop, the coming years will be decisive in strengthening Central Asia\'s position as an independent and influential actor within the <\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">evolving<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> global climate architecture.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">An important milestone in this process is the Regional Environmental Summit in Astana. The summit is intended not only to assess the progress achieved over the past decade but <\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">also to establish a long-term roadmap for technological modernization across the region. It is expected to institutionalize the operational framework of the Central Asian Climate Fund, transforming environmental initiatives into viable investment projects.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Looking ahead, the regional environmental agenda is likely to revolve around three strategic priorities.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">First, technological sovereignty.<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> Central Asia will increasingly seek to move beyond importing environmental technologies toward developing and localizing its own solutions, including smart water management systems and digital emissions monitoring for thermal power plants.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Second, the greening of the economy.<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> ESG standards are expected to become progressively integrated into the operations of national companies, improving access to green finance while maintaining export competitiveness under the expanding carbon regulation mechanisms of international markets.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Third, policy coordination.<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> Acting as a cohesive regional climate bloc at future COP conferences will enable Central Asian countries to more effectively advocate for their common interests, particularly with regard to international support for climate adaptation initiatives.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"><i>Conclusion<\\/i><\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Environmental policy in Central Asia has decisively evolved from a predominantly humanitarian concern into a strategic pillar of regional development.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;border-left:none;border-top:none;border-right:none;border-bottom:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">The region\'s experience demonstrates that <\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">transboundary<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> environmental challenges are best addressed not through competition but through cooperation and synergy. This approach offers compelling evidence that Central Asia is no l<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">onger merely perceived as a region vulnerable to climate risks. Instead, it is increasingly emerging as a space of opportunity, where a new model of sustainable development is taking shapeÔÇöone that could serve as an example for the broader Eurasian region.<\\/span><\\/p>\"}',19,'{\"uz\":\"\",\"ru\":\"\",\"en\":\"\"}'),
('ms2v8d4tpw55','{\"uz\":\"Raqamli texnologiyalar va sanoat kooperatsiyasi Germaniya va Markaziy Osiyo o╩╗rtasidagi hamkorlikning harakatlantiruvchi kuchiga aylanishi mumkin\",\"ru\":\"ºĞº©ªäªÇº¥º▓ªïºÁ ªéºÁªàº¢º¥º╗º¥º│º©º© º© º┐ªÇº¥º╝º║º¥º¥º┐ºÁªÇº░ªåº©ªÅ º╝º¥º│ªâªé ªüªéº░ªéªî º┤ªÇº░º╣º▓ºÁªÇº░º╝º© ªüº¥ªéªÇªâº┤º¢º©ªçºÁªüªéº▓º░ ºôºÁªÇº╝º░º¢º©º© º© ºĞºÁº¢ªéªÇº░º╗ªîº¢º¥º╣ ºÉºÀº©º©\",\"en\":\"Digital technologies and industrial cooperation can become drivers of cooperation between Germany and Central Asia\"}','Hisobot','Tashqi siyosat','Global','','2026','published','uploads/img_20260727_084654_1bfef3b4.jpg','uploads/doc_20260728_064929_ec58003f.pdf','{\"uz\":\"<p style=\\\"text-indent:35.400000000000006pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\" class=\\\"docData;DOCY;v5;38681;\\\\/BEAEOARPBEIEOAQ1BCAAMQRLBDsEPgQgAD4EQAQzBDAEPQQ4BDcEPgQyBDAEPQQ+BCAAGAQ9BEEEQgQ4BEIEQwRCBD4EPAQgAEEEQgRABDAEQgQ1BDMEOARHBDUEQQQ6BDgERQQgADgEIAA8BDUENgRABDUEMwQ4BD4EPQQwBDsETAQ9BEsERQQgADgEQQRBBDsENQQ0BD4EMgQwBD0EOAQ5BCAAPwRABDgEIAA\\\\\\\\/BDUEQAQyBEsERQQsACAATQRCBD4EIAAF1QAAAAFAAAAABAYOAAAAQwBhAG0AYgByAGkAYQAFBg4AAABDAGEAbQBiAHIAaQBhAAgEHAAAAA0GBgAAADYAOQA5ABYEHAAAAAiLAAAAAIYAAAA\\\\\\\\\\/wEAAAD6AQAAEgQ+BC0AMgRCBD4EQARLBEUELAAgAE0EOgQ+BD0EPgQ8BDgERwQ1BEEEOgQwBE8EIAA4BCAAQgQ1BEUEPQQ+BDsEPgQzBDgERwQ1BEEEOgQwBE8EIAA6BD4EPgQ\\/BDUEQAQwBEYEOARPBC4AIAAhBD4EMgQ+BDoEQwQ\\/BD0ESwQ5BCAAQgQ+BDIEMARABD4EPgQxBD4EQAQ+BEIEIAA8BDUENgQ0BEMEIAATBDUEQAQ8BDAEPQQ4BDUEOQQgADgEIABBBEIEQAQwBD0EMAQ8BDgEIAAmBDUEPQRCBEAEMAQ7BEwEPQQ+BDkEIAAQBDcEOAQ4BCAANAQ+BEEEQgQ4BDMEIAA\\\\/BDAEQARCBD0EUQRABD4EMgQgAEAENQQzBDgEPgQ9BDAEIAAyBCAAFQQhBCwAIAAwBCAARwQ4BEEEOwQ+BCAAPwRABDUENAQ\\/BEAEOARPBEIEOAQ5BCAAQQQgAD0ENQQ8BDUERgQ6BDgEPAQgADoEMAQ\\/BDgEQgQwBDsEPgQ8BCAAPwRABDUEMgRLBEgEMAQ1BEIEIAAxADMAMAAwAC4AIAASBCAAIwQ3BDEENQQ6BDgEQQRCBDAEP