ttom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\" class=\\\"docData;DOCY;v5;31821;\\\\\\\\\\\\/ACAAVwBoAGEAdAAgAGEAZAB2AGEAbgB0AGEAZwBlAHMAIABjAG8AdQBsAGQAIAB0AGgAaQBzACAAcAByAG8AdgBpAGQAZQA\\\\\\\\\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Digita<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">l technologies, industrial cooperation, green energy, and human capital are emerging as new drivers of cooperation between Central Asia and Germany. These issues were at the center of discussions during the First Central AsiaÔÇôGermany Expert Forum, held in <\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Khiva<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> on 16ÔÇô17 April.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">The event was jointly organized by the Institute for Strategic and Regional Studies under the President of the Republic of Uzbekistan, the <\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Konrad<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> Adenauer Foundation, and the Friedrich Ebert Foundation.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Gazeta<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">.<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">uz<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> spoke with <\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"><b>Daria<\\/b><\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"><b> <\\/b><\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"><b>Gorelkina<\\/b><\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">, <\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"><i>Chief Research Fellow at the Center for Foreign Policy Studies and International Initiatives<\\/i><\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">, about the key areas that are expected to shape GermanyÔÇôCentral Asia cooperation in the coming years.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"><b>ÔÇô <\\/b><\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"><b>Which areas of political dialogue between Central Asia and Germany should become priorities in the medium term? What makes these areas particularly important? <\\/b><\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">In the medium term, three priority areas stand out.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">First, support for institutional development across the countries of Central Asia. For decades, Germany has been a consistent strategic partner, facilitating the transfer of expertise in public administration and p<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">roviding advisory support in implementing international legal standards. Intensive intergovernmental dialogue has also created a solid foundation for expanding bilateral relations and coordinating efforts across the full spectrum of the partnership agenda.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Second, economic and technological cooperation.<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> Total trade between Germany and the Central Asian countries has reached approximately Ôé¼11 billion, more than tripling compared to 2017. Germany is now among the European Union\'s principal trade and economic partner<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">s in the region, while the number of companies with German capital operating in Central Asia exceeds 1,300. In Uzbekistan alone, accumulated German investment is estimated at US$1ÔÇô1.5 billion, primarily concentrated in industry, energy, and infrastructure.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">These indicators reflect the steady expansion of economic interdependence and provide a solid basis for moving toward more sophisticated forms of cooperation, including industrial partnerships, <\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">production localization, green energy development, and enhanced transport connectivity.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Third, strengthening multilateral cooperation.<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> <\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">As the international system undergoes profound transformation, there is a growing need to align strategic approaches and shift toward more practical, results-oriented formats of cooperation, including closer coordination within international organizations.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">On which international issues do the positions of Central Asian countries and Germany largely coincide? Where do differences remain?<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">On most major global issues, our approaches are remarkably similar. Both Central Asia and Germany remain firmly committed to multilateralism in addressing global challenges such as climate change and the green transition.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Economically, both sides share an interest in developing international transport corridors, securing access to critical raw materials, and advancing industrial and digital technologies.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">The remaining differences primarily stem from Germany\'s unique position as Europe\'s leading economy and as a member of both the European Union and NATO, as wel<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">l as from its highly advanced level of economic development. Central Asia, by contrast, remains a developing region. As a result, perspectives may differ regarding the pace of the energy transition, approaches to geo-economic policy, and attitudes toward i<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">nternational sanctions regimes.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">However, these differences are relatively limited in scope and do not impede the strategic dialogue between our countries.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"><b>ÔÇô <\\/b><\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"><b>Do you believe that Central Asian countries should develop a coordinated regional approach to attracting investment from Germany and Europe more broadly? What advantages could this provide?<\\/b><\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Yes. Developing a coordinated regional investment strategy could significantly enhance Central Asia\'s attractiveness as an investment destination.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">By combining the economic potential of its individual states, the region creates a cumulati<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">ve scale effect, transforming itself into a larger, more transparent market of strategic interest to German investors. Coordinated macroeconomic policies also help reduce investment risks, lower market-entry barriers, and improve regulatory predictability.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">This is particularly important for capital-intensive infrastructure and energy projects, where cross-border cooperation and substantial long-term investment are essential.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Such an approach would establish a strong foundation for long-term technological partnership while substantially expanding the presence of leading German companies throughout the region.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"><b>ÔÇô <\\/b><\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"><b>Are the priorities of German investors being analyzed at either the national or regional level? To what extent do their interests coincide with the development priorities of Central Asian countries?<\\/b><\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Yes. Such analyses are conducted both by relevant government instit<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">utions and by the business community itself. Encouragingly, business associations have become increasingly active in recent years, maintaining constructive dialogue with public authorities and offering practical proposals to improve the investment climate.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">German investors primarily focus on manufacturing, energy, transport and logistics, as well as environmentally sustainable technologies. Germany has been particularly active in promoting renewable energy and energy-efficiency projects.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">These priorities closely correspond to the long-term development strategies of Central Asian countries.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">At<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> the same time, several challenges remain, particularly regarding the institutional environment, investment protection, and regulatory predictability. Comprehensive efforts are underway to address these issues and further accelerate investment cooperation.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\">&nbsp;<\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"><b>ÔÇô<\\/b><\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Calibri\';font-size:11pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> <\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"><b>Which areas of cooperation between Germany and Central Asia still offer the greatest untapped potential?<\\/b><\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">The greatest untapped potential lies in several closely interconnected sectors.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">First, digital technologies, particularly artificial intelligence, where opportunities exist to establish joint technological platforms and innovation ecosystems.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Second, industrial cooperation.<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> Rising energy costs in Germany are increasing interest in relocating certain manufacturing activities abroad, including to Central Asia, where competitive advantages are becoming increasingly evident.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Third, human capital.<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\"> Germany faces a growing shortage of skilled labor, while Central Asi<\\/span><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">a has one of the world\'s youngest and fastest-growing populations. This creates a highly complementary partnership: Central Asia can contribute human resources, while Germany can provide advanced education, vocational training, and technological expertise.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;mso-border-left-alt:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;mso-border-right-alt:none;mso-border-bottom-alt:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">There is also considerable potential at the intersection of climate policy, water resource management, and energy, where integrated regional solutions are increasingly necessary.<\\/span><\\/p><p style=\\\"text-indent:35.45pt;text-align:justify;line-height:120%;margin-top:6.000000000000001pt;margin-bottom:6.000000000000001pt;border:none;border-left:none;border-top:none;border-right:none;border-bottom:none;mso-border-between:none\\\"><span style=\\\"font-family:\'Cambria\';font-size:14pt;color:#000000;mso-style-textfill-fill-color:#000000\\\">Finally, substantial opportunities remain in expanding trade, strengthening transport connectivity, and developing regional value chains capable of generating higher value-added production.<\\/span><\\/p>\"}',22,'{\"uz\":\"\",\"ru\":\"\",\"en\":\"\"}'),
